From e61fc90d81ec2f79d5d9713811efa29ae177c34d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:22:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix/video-attach-idempotent: teardown owns the tile; the
 sweep fires on roster change only

Diagnosis (see previous commit) showed the attach path already idempotent
(1 assignment / 1 creation / 0 re-parents per stable participant) but the
disagreement sweep ran 82 times in a 60s episode (every reflow) and its
bare el.remove() left VIDEO_TILES entries dangling with a live srcObject
(the passed-but-still-in-call man) - gate 08's orphan.

The fix:
- releaseTile(sid,{stop}) is THE tile teardown: element removal, entry
  release, and (for the sweep) stopping the stream are one operation.
  onTrackStopped / onPartLeft / foreign-feed eviction / cell moves all go
  through it - no bare remove() anywhere.
- placeVideo: same-track early return stands; a genuine stream change is
  one in-place assignment; a genuine cell move is keyed reconciliation
  (static cells, fresh mount, never a re-parent - Safari restarts
  playback when a <video> changes parents).
- sweepVideo extracted from reflowVideo, gated on the participant->tile
  map signature: it fires on roster CHANGE only, a reflow storm with an
  unchanged map is a no-op, and a pending 6s disagreement window gets
  exactly one one-shot recheck (no interval, nothing calls play()).

After, same 60s episode: sweeps 82 -> 13, dangling entries 1 -> 0,
counters still 1/1/0 per participant.  Gate 08-video-life now passes
unmodified; new gate 13-reattach-budget scores the whole episode against
the budget via the app's own counters.

